The function must: (1) be named `flatten`, (2) accept a nested list of arbitrary depth, (3) use recursion or an iterative approach to handle any nesting level, (4) return a flat list. A correct implementation: def flatten(lst):
    result = []
    for item in lst:
        if isinstance(item, list):
            result.extend(flatten(item))
        else:
            result.append(item)
    return result

The decorator must: (1) be named `memoize`, (2) maintain a cache (e.g., a dictionary), (3) use the function arguments as cache keys, (4) return cached results on repeated calls, (5) work with any function. Example implementation: def memoize(func):
    cache = {}
    def wrapper(*args):
        if args not in cache:
            cache[args] = func(*args)
        return cache[args]
    return wrapper

